{"step_index":97,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:52:22Z","thinking":"**Examining Notification Reset Record**\n\nThe record details a notification reset, dubbed \"Sunday Room,\" deployed in July. It offers an option for weekly digests to workspace admins, a change from the legacy daily contributor subscriptions. This provides key context for understanding potential notification-related issues.\n\n\n**Connecting Legacy Subscriptions & Tickets**\n\nThe support ticket describes a contributor receiving daily digests, despite the UI indicating a weekly option. This points to the earlier notification reset, specifically the change where contributor-level daily subscriptions weren't migrated. It seems legacy daily subscriptions are still active for individual contributors, and not migrated to the weekly option. This explains why the user, a contributor, is still receiving the daily digest.\n\n\n**Investigating Incorrect Assumptions & Rollback**\n\nThe initial assessment of the notification system was incomplete, as \"Sunday Room\" changes only applied to workspace administrators. Contributor subscriptions were not migrated.\n\nThe \"Focus Shelf\" feature was rolled back due to slow query performance, specifically in workspaces with a high number of tasks. Initial usage metrics were flawed because automation accounts skewed the data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 /workspace/skill/scripts/history.py search /workspace/product \"record-764afbf446\" \"record-d4f34a4dc1\" \"record-e36f0fe1aa\" \"record-5f1a34c149\" --limit 10","Cwd":"/workspace","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Search for specific receipts and ticket IDs"}}]}
