{"step_index":115,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:52:51Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Long-Horizon Skill Details**\n\nInitial focus on using specified data for the handoff review. Determine if \"status filters on phone\" and \"quieter digest\" are viable improvements for this week. Need to examine past attempts, outcomes, and next steps for both suggestions within the product context.\n\n\n**Evaluating Onboarding Improvements**\n\nInitial assessment suggests no specific week is identified for the onboarding improvements, but \"status filters on phone\" and \"quieter digest\" are viable candidates. Checking for prior actions and outcomes related to these improvement ideas in the available records, to assess their historical context and feasibility for next steps. Determining how previous attempts were terminated will inform whether to consider them again.\n\n\n**Examining Mobile Status Filters**\n\nPast attempts at status filters (Focus Shelf) were restricted to desktop and encountered performance issues on large workspaces. The original usage report incorrectly included automation accounts, skewing the usage data. Evaluating if the performance issues are resolvable, as mobile was excluded from the previous experiment.\n\n**Considering Digest Quieter Options**\n\nThe second feedback item pertains to a \"quieter digest\". No specific prior action on this topic exists in the records. Determining the exact meaning of \"quieter\" in this context is the first priority.\n\n\n**Re-evaluating Desktop Feature Outcomes**\n\nThe August release included an architectural fix that resolved desktop performance bottlenecks. The September activity report revision shows 21% human weekly usage, debunking a \"low use\" misconception. This usage data needs to be considered in conjunction with prior mobile status information which explicitly states no mobile availability.\n\n**Analyzing \"Quieter Digest\" Feedback**\n\nFeedback suggests a